难道不是美妙绝伦吗？
Isn't the Isle of Man
just amazing?

521
00:28:23,167 --> 00:28:24,233
哎呀，简直棒绝了。
Why, it's fabulous.

522
00:28:24,267 --> 00:28:25,667
就像有人专门去
It's like somebody's
gone out and designed

523
00:28:25,700 --> 00:28:27,500
设计了一座《Top Gear》梦幻岛，
Top Gear fantasy island,

524
00:28:27,533 --> 00:28:28,800
专供我们享乐一样。
especially for us.

525
00:28:28,833 --> 00:28:32,167
我可是彻底被那儿的腌熏鲱鱼迷住了。
I was absolutely blown away
by those kippers.

526
00:28:32,200 --> 00:28:33,967
-没错。
-他这一路就没聊过别的！
-Yes.
-That's all he's been
talking about.

527
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:36,167
“詹姆斯，这儿可不限速！”
“哦，那熏鲱鱼味道如何？”
"There's no
speed limits here, James."
"Oh, what about the kippers."

528
00:28:36,200 --> 00:28:38,000
不过我还真想再来一条熏鲱鱼。
I'd love another
kipper though.

529
00:28:38,033 --> 00:28:41,100
我还从没开过一辆
开起来和长相差别如此巨大的车。
I've never driven a car
that drives so differently
to the way it looks.

530
00:28:41,133 --> 00:28:43,233
因为那根本就不是什么四门轿车。
'Cause that is not
a four-seater saloon.

531
00:28:43,267 --> 00:28:46,533
它就是披着轿车壳子的纯种赛车，
太绝了。
It's a race car
with that body on top of it.
It's brilliant.

532
00:28:46,567 --> 00:28:49,267
跑在那些路上，简直是完美无瑕。
And on those roads,
it was just perfection.

533
00:28:49,300 --> 00:28:50,667
是啊，全都很棒。
Yeah, they're all great.

534
00:28:50,700 --> 00:28:53,667
确实，我喜欢宝马M系，
我也喜欢曼岛。
I do, I like the M cars.
And I like the Isle of Man.

535
00:28:53,667 --> 00:28:55,100
不过遗憾的是，我今晚的嘉宾，
Sadly, though,
my guest tonight,

536
00:28:55,133 --> 00:28:56,500
我想他这辈子恐怕都没法去那儿。
I don't think he can
ever have gone there.

537
00:28:56,533 --> 00:28:58,400
因为他要是去了，非得被抽桦条鞭子不可。
Because if he did,
he'd be birched.

538
00:28:58,433 --> 00:29:00,833
女士们先生们，
史蒂芬·弗莱！
Ladies and gentlemen,
Stephen Fry.

539
00:29:00,867 --> 00:29:02,333
（欢呼喝彩）
(CHEERING)

540
00:29:03,267 --> 00:29:05,533
非常感谢。
Thank you very much.

541
00:29:05,567 --> 00:29:07,700
-你好吗？
-很好，谢谢你，非常棒。
-How are you?
-Fine, thank you.
Very good.

542
00:29:07,733 --> 00:29:08,800
请坐。
Take a seat.

543
00:29:12,667 --> 00:29:14,533
-你去过曼岛吗？
-去过。
-Have you been
to the Isle of Man?
-Yes.

544
00:29:14,567 --> 00:29:16,800
你到了机场说：“我爱曼岛（爱男人）。”
You go to the airport,
you say, "I love man."

545
00:29:16,833 --> 00:29:18,833
他们就会说：
“在这儿你休想爱。”
And they say,
"Not here, you don't."

546
00:29:18,867 --> 00:29:21,467
-这……我得解释一下……
-在那是违法的。
-It is... I should explain...
-It is illegal to love man.

547
00:29:21,500 --> 00:29:23,467
-在“男人岛”。
-以前是违法的。
-In the "Isle of Man".
-It was illegal.

548
00:29:23,500 --> 00:29:25,933
在那儿“爱男人”是会被抽鞭子的。
And you could be birched
for loving man there.

549
00:29:25,967 --> 00:29:29,167
是啊，而在伦敦
好多人可是要花大价钱买这项“服务”的。
Yes, which is something
people pay a lot of money for
in London.

550
00:29:29,200 --> 00:29:30,833
所以在那儿就跟免费福利一样。
So it's like a free service.

551
00:29:30,867 --> 00:29:33,433
那真是个奇葩的地方，对吧？
你在那儿呆的时间长吗？
It's a peculiar place,
isn't it? You've spent
much time there?

552
00:29:33,467 --> 00:29:36,033
挺长的，其实我经常去。
Yeah, I go there
quite a lot, actually.

553
00:29:36,067 --> 00:29:39,667
他们那里的某些法律简直神了。
Some of the laws
they have are fabulous.

554
00:29:39,667 --> 00:29:42,133
比如说手枪，
在那儿居然是合法的。
Handguns,
for instance,
are legal there.

555
00:29:42,167 --> 00:29:44,700
而且你还可能被指控“狂暴驾驶罪”。
And you could be charged
with furious driving.

556
00:29:44,733 --> 00:29:46,733
我做梦都想在驾照上印上这么一条罪名！
I'd love to have that
on my licence!

557
00:29:46,767 --> 00:29:48,500
（大笑）“狂暴驾驶”！
(LAUGHING) Furious driving!

558
00:29:48,533 --> 00:29:51,700
你很渴望那种自由吗？
Do you hanker after
that kind of freedom?

559
00:29:51,733 --> 00:29:53,833
嗯，某种程度上我算个左派，
Well, I'm a sort of
leftie in a way,

560
00:29:53,867 --> 00:29:58,300
但我真的无法向你形容那种排山倒海的痛恨，
那种阵阵翻涌的恶心，
but I cannot tell you the
overmastering hatred I feel,
the waves of disgust,

561
00:29:58,333 --> 00:30:01,367
路上总有个骑自行车的女人
皱着眉头瞪着你，
when there is that
frowning woman on the bicycle,

562
00:30:01,400 --> 00:30:05,667
那眼神就好像
你就是资本主义、大鱼大肉，
who looks at you as if
you are the symbol of all
capitalism and meat-eating,

563
00:30:05,700 --> 00:30:07,300
以及长了命根子的万恶象征……
and penis-owning...

564
00:30:07,333 --> 00:30:09,700
你懂的，仿佛你就是人民公敌，
You know, you are
the enemy of the people,

565
00:30:09,733 --> 00:30:12,500
是地球的死对头，
是全球化毒瘤，
you are the enemy
of the planet,
you are globalisation,

566
00:30:12,533 --> 00:30:14,533
是叼着大雪茄的万恶资本家，
you are capitalism
with a huge cigar,

567
00:30:14,567 --> 00:30:18,667
就因为你开车带过的一阵风，
稍微吹歪了她那该死的破自行车。
just because you might have
slightly blown her off course
on her blasted bicycle.

568
00:30:18,700 --> 00:30:20,267
你见过那种人吧？
You know that kind?

569
00:30:20,300 --> 00:30:22,933
然而……
然而这些套在你头上完全不对劲，
And yet...
And yet none of this is
kind of ringing true,

570
00:30:22,967 --> 00:30:26,900
-因为据我所知，
你今天开来的车……
-天呐。
-because I know that
the car you drive today...
-Oh, dear.

571
00:30:26,933 --> 00:30:28,567
-……其实是一辆萨博。
-对，没错。
-...it is a Saab.
-Yeah, right.

572
00:30:28,600 --> 00:30:31,667
但你发现没有，
你这辈子绝不可能听见
有人说：
Now, do you know something,
you will never hear
anyone say,

573
00:30:31,700 --> 00:30:33,200
“看开萨博的那个疯子！”
"Look at that maniac
in that Saab."

574
00:30:33,233 --> 00:30:35,233
（笑声）
确实如此。
(LAUGHING)
That's true.

575
00:30:35,267 --> 00:30:39,000
开萨博的人可以说是
全马路上车品最好的了。
Saabs are the most
beautifully driven cars
on the roads.

576
00:30:39,033 --> 00:30:40,200
我们下周正好要测一辆，
We're gonna review one,
next week,

577
00:30:40,233 --> 00:30:42,333
因为我实在太好奇了，
because I'm fascinated
to find out

578
00:30:42,367 --> 00:30:45,467
人一旦坐进萨博里到底会中什么邪，
能瞬间变得那么……
what happens to you
when you climb in a Saab
that suddenly you become...

579
00:30:45,500 --> 00:30:48,533
这确实很邪门，
你说得一点没错。
It's peculiar,
you're quite right.

580
00:30:48,567 --> 00:30:50,600
但我不得不坦白，
我骨子里是个飙车狂，
But I have to confess,
I am a speed merchant

581
00:30:50,633 --> 00:30:53,967
好几次差一点就把驾照给扣没了。
and I have come so close
to losing my licence.

582
00:30:54,000 --> 00:30:55,933
差不多正好一年前，
Almost exactly a year ago,

583
00:30:55,967 --> 00:31:01,667
我在M11高速上慢悠悠兜风，
时速一百……（清嗓子）
英里每小时。
I was pootling along the M11
at 100 and... (CLEARS THROAT)
Miles per hour.

584
00:31:01,667 --> 00:31:05,300
幸好交警测的是区间均速，
结果是99.8。
And fortunately
they took an average,
which was 99.8.

585
00:31:05,333 --> 00:31:08,100
均速？从你刚坐进车里开始算的？
An average from when
you got into the car?

586
00:31:08,133 --> 00:31:11,300
对，没错，
从伦敦市中心一路算起。
Yes, quite,
from the centre of London.

587
00:31:11,333 --> 00:31:13,567
讲真，太阳打西边出来
才会有车超我。
It's a rare day I'm overtaken,
to be honest.

588
00:31:13,667 --> 00:31:15,833
我也不知道图什么，
真挺可悲的。
I don't know what it is.
It's pathetic.

589
00:31:15,867 --> 00:31:20,233
不是幼稚、虚荣，
就是好胜心作祟，
It's either infantile,
or vanity,
or competitiveness,

590
00:31:20,267 --> 00:31:23,000
往好听了说，
就是极度耐不住无聊。
or it is at best,
a low boredom threshold.

591
00:31:23,033 --> 00:31:27,200
所以你得时刻保持神经紧绷，
整个人才能不犯困。
And so, you wanna keep
just being on edge all the
time, so that you're awake.

592
00:31:27,233 --> 00:31:30,033
而且你很出名的一点，
就是你还拥有一辆伦敦出租车。
And you're of course
also famed for having
a London cab.

593
00:31:30,067 --> 00:31:31,967
-对，是的。
-专门在伦敦市里开吗？
-Yes, yeah.
-Is that for use in London?

594
00:31:32,000 --> 00:31:33,700
那当然，纯粹是出于实用考虑。
Surely, yes,
a purely practical decision.

595
00:31:33,733 --> 00:31:38,033
我当时琢磨着，
毕竟经常要在伦敦城里到处穿梭，
I just thought eventually,
you know, driving around
London I did,

596
00:31:38,067 --> 00:31:40,967
我又放弃了开越野摩托。
I'd given up having
a trail bike.

597
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:42,167
你？骑摩托车？！
You on a motor bike?

598
00:31:42,200 --> 00:31:44,000
是啊，我知道很滑稽。
骑起来老是晃晃悠悠的……
Yes, I know.
It used to turn wobbly...

599
00:31:44,033 --> 00:31:46,667
这场面……
花钱我都想买票开开眼。
That's something...
I would have paid
to watch that.

600
00:31:46,700 --> 00:31:51,867
我有个堂兄在纽约当外科医生
I had a cousin who was
a surgeon in New York

601
00:31:51,900 --> 00:31:53,967
在急诊室，
或者照他们的叫法，
创伤科。
in the Casualty
or Trauma Department,
as they call it.

602
00:31:54,000 --> 00:31:57,700
我们碰巧坐了同一班飞机，
下机后在一家餐馆碰了面。
And I was in a plane
and we met afterwards
at a restaurant.

603
00:31:57,733 --> 00:32:00,367
他见我寄存摩托头盔，便说：
He saw me checking-in
my skidlid and he said,

604
00:32:00,400 --> 00:32:02,333
-“我怎么不知道你还骑摩托？”
-我说：“是啊。”
-"I didn't know
you rode a bike."
-I said, "Yeah."

605
00:32:02,367 --> 00:32:06,567
他说：“你知道我们创伤科
管骑摩托车的人叫什么吗？
He said, "Do you know
what we call motor bike riders
in the Trauma Department,

606
00:32:06,667 --> 00:32:09,367
-就是罗斯福医院里。”
-我说：“叫什么？”
-"in the Roosevelt Hospital?"
-I said, "No."

607
00:32:09,400 --> 00:32:11,167
“器官捐献者。”
"Donors."

608
00:32:11,200 --> 00:32:14,133
我心想这可不是什么好兆头。
诡异的是，一周后，
It's a bad sign, I thought.
Then, weirdly, a week later,

609
00:32:14,167 --> 00:32:16,067
我去探望一位朋友，
他的姑妈
I'm seeing to a friend of mine
who had an aunt

610
00:32:16,100 --> 00:32:20,400
刚去穆尔菲尔兹眼科医院
做白内障手术。
who'd gone into
Moorfields Hospital for one
of those cataract operations.

611
00:32:20,433 --> 00:32:22,433
医生搓着双手走进来，
说道：
And the doctor came in
rubbing his hands
and said,

612
00:32:22,467 --> 00:32:27,067
“好了，史密斯太太，”
他说，“流程想必都跟您解释过了。
"Well, now, Mrs Smith,"
he said, "I'm sure it's all
been explained to you.

613
00:32:27,100 --> 00:32:29,533
我们把那颗浑浊的老白内障切掉，
"We cut out that
cloudy old cataract

614
00:32:29,567 --> 00:32:34,833
再缝上一枚漂亮、新鲜、
闪闪发光的供体晶状体。
"and we sew in a nice, new,
fresh, sparkly donor lens.

615
00:32:34,867 --> 00:32:37,367
只可惜，眼下我们
一个供体晶状体都没有。”
"Unfortunately, we don't
have any donor lenses
at the moment."

616
00:32:37,400 --> 00:32:41,433
接着他走到窗前说：“不过外面下雨了，
估计用不了多久就会有了。”
And he went to the window
and said, "but it's raining,
so it shouldn't be too long."

617
00:32:41,967 --> 00:32:43,667
而且他是说真的。
And he really meant it.

618
00:32:43,667 --> 00:32:46,367
总之，这件事最终
让我彻底戒了摩托车。
Anyway, that stopped me
from riding a motorbike,
eventually.

619
00:32:46,400 --> 00:32:48,333
-再加上被吊销驾照。
-那为什么买出租车？
-That and being banned.
-So why a cab?

620
00:32:48,367 --> 00:32:52,200
哎，我当时就想……
骑摩托进城确实很方便，
Well, I just thought it's...
The bike would be a great way
of getting into town

621
00:32:52,233 --> 00:32:55,733
能飞快赶到市中心
去录配音什么的。
to do voiceovers
and the things in the centre
of the town, quickly.

622
00:32:55,767 --> 00:32:58,900
后来我觉得换成汽车……
好吧，我现在必须得有辆车了。
And I thought a car...
I've got to have a car now,
all right.

623
00:32:58,933 --> 00:33:02,333
我又不住在地铁站附近，
天天打车又贵得离谱。
I wasn't near a tube station
and a cab seemed ridiculous.

624
00:33:02,367 --> 00:33:06,167
然后我灵机一动：
“但要是自己买辆出租车呢……”
Then I thought,
"My own cab,
on the other hand..."

625
00:33:06,200 --> 00:33:08,933
虽说在大庭广众之下
我绝不会承认自己走公交车道，
Not that I would admit to
using bus lanes in public,

626
00:33:08,967 --> 00:33:10,833
毕竟没有出租车运营牌照
那是违法的。
'cause it's illegal
if you're not
a licensed cabbie.

627
00:33:10,867 --> 00:33:13,500
但咱们面对现实吧，
公交车道就在那儿摆着。
But let's face it,
they do exist, bus lanes.

628
00:33:13,533 --> 00:33:15,867
-只要你开着出租车，就能直接走。
-只要你开着出租车。
-And you can drive in them
if you have a cab.
-If you have a cab.

629
00:33:15,900 --> 00:33:17,733
谁会去查你车牌啊。
Who's gonna check
the registration plate.

630
00:33:17,767 --> 00:33:19,367
而且别的出租车还会主动给你让路。
And the other cabs let you in.

631
00:33:19,400 --> 00:33:22,767
我把这叫做
“的哥情谊”。
You know, cab-eraderie,
I call it.

632
00:33:22,800 --> 00:33:25,700
碰到大多数私家车，
你只要把手往车窗外一招，
And most cars, you know,
you just stick your hand
out of the window

633
00:33:25,733 --> 00:33:29,300
就能一把变道切进车流里。
这才是真正的天大好处。
and you move out into traffic.
I mean that's the real gain.

634
00:33:29,333 --> 00:33:33,100
但这很奇怪，因为
我认识的大多数懂拉丁语的人，
But it's strange, because
most of the people I know
who speak Latin

635
00:33:33,133 --> 00:33:36,333
都觉得汽车特别俗气、特别幼稚。
find cars really rather
trivial and infantile.

636
00:33:36,367 --> 00:33:40,667
是的……我觉得……
就普遍偏见而言，你说得没错，
Yes... I think...
I mean, as a generalisation,
I suppose you're right

637
00:33:40,700 --> 00:33:45,567
我这身粗花呢西装
怎么看都不像是个狂热车迷。
that this tweed does not
bespeak someone
who loves cars.

638
00:33:45,667 --> 00:33:48,133
大家经常对我说：
“斯蒂芬，你生错了时代吧？”
People often say to me,
"Stephen, you were born in
the wrong age, weren't you?"

639
00:33:48,167 --> 00:33:50,667
“你应该活在维多利亚全盛期，
或是当个摄政时期的花花公子，
You would have loved
to be in a high Victorian
or a Regency dandy

640
00:33:50,700 --> 00:33:53,700
再不然也得是伊丽莎白时代什么的”，
这纯属胡说八道。
or an Elizabethian
or something, and it's
absolute nonsense.

641
00:33:53,733 --> 00:33:57,700
我是说，能活在人类
各项成就集大成的时代，
I mean, I think, to live
at the summation of human
achievement in everything

642
00:33:57,733 --> 00:34:01,067
从计算机到内燃机，
这简直太美妙了，
from computing to the internal
combustion engine
is a wonderful thing,

643
00:34:01,100 --> 00:34:04,433
因为我们知晓过去。
如果你是维多利亚时代的人，你可以去想象过去，
because we've got
the past age, you can imagine
if you're a Victorian.

644
00:34:04,467 --> 00:34:07,400
但若是维多利亚时代的人，
你根本无法想象
生活在20世纪70年代是什么样，
But if you're a Victorian,
you couldn't imagine
you lived in the 1970s.

645
00:34:07,433 --> 00:34:09,400
更无法想象
生活在90年代。
You couldn't imagine
you lived in the 1990s.

646
00:34:09,433 --> 00:34:13,967
最妙的是，
我们正处于万事万物的
绝对巅峰。
And the beauty of it is,
we are at the absolute peak
of everything.

647
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:17,433
就在我们说话的这一分这一秒，
是有史以来
最现代的一刻。
As we speak, this minute
is the most modern minute
that ever happened.

648
00:34:17,467 --> 00:34:22,500
但你这么说，
可我们现在聊天的当口，
才过去多久，才不过一周左右——
But then you say that,
we are speaking,
what, just a week or so after

649
00:34:22,533 --> 00:34:24,933
-航空领域才刚刚倒退了一步。
-你说的对。
-we went over it
in terms of aviation.
-You're right.

650
00:34:24,967 --> 00:34:28,067
这可是极其罕见的事情。
谁能想到
会发生这种事？
That is one of the rarest
events. Whoever thought
this would happen?

651
00:34:28,100 --> 00:34:33,200
我是说，极少有什么事物
在登上顶峰之后，
突然开始走下坡路，
I mean, there are few things
like that we've crested and
suddenly we're going backwards

652
00:34:33,233 --> 00:34:35,667
这在近现代历史上
是非常罕见的事。
and that's a very rare event
in recent history.

653
00:34:35,667 --> 00:34:39,233
上一次大倒退，我能想到的
还是公元410年罗马人撤离不列颠。
I can't think of another time
since the Romans left in 410.

654
00:34:39,267 --> 00:34:41,167
-没错，确实如此。
-整整一千六百年啊。
-Yeah, that's right.
-1600 years.

655
00:34:41,200 --> 00:34:45,133
我们把抽水马桶的文明美德
抛弃了整整七百年。
真是不可思议。
We abandoned the virtues
of the lavatory for 700 years.
That's extraordinary.

656
00:34:45,167 --> 00:34:47,000
-可不是嘛。
-直接往窗外拉屎。
-It is.
-Pooed out of the window.

657
00:34:47,033 --> 00:34:49,900
话说回来，你以前有一大批
汽车收藏，对吧？
'Cause you had
a big car collection,
didn't you, at one point?

658
00:34:49,933 --> 00:34:52,933
是的，我曾经有过八九辆，
清一色全是英国车。
Yes, I had eight or nine
entirely British cars.

659
00:34:52,967 --> 00:34:58,100
听起来又是一副
老派粗花呢绅士的调调。
都是些奇奇怪怪的玩意儿，比如……
Which again seems
to sound very tweedy.
They were odd things, like...

660
00:34:58,133 --> 00:35:00,233
我买过一辆沃尔斯利 15/50（Wolseley 15/50），
I had a Wolseley 15/50,

661
00:35:00,267 --> 00:35:03,367
就是那种老警车，
车标还会发光的那款，
which is that sort of
police car, the one with
the badge that lights up,

662
00:35:03,400 --> 00:35:05,033
带着个笔挺的小遮阳板。
in the straight little visor.

663
00:35:05,067 --> 00:35:08,800
还有一辆MG Magnette，
就是宾尼法利纳操刀的那款，
你懂的。
And an MG Magnette,
one of those Pininfarina ones,
you know.

664
00:35:08,833 --> 00:35:11,300
还有一辆奥斯汀·希利 100-6（Austin Healey 100-6），
And an Austin Healey 100-6,

665
00:35:11,333 --> 00:35:14,133
那车漂亮极了，
冰蓝配象牙白。
which is a gorgeous car,
ice blue over ivory.

666
00:35:14,167 --> 00:35:17,533
依我看，听着你分明就是
在苦苦怀念那个旧时代嘛。
To me, it does sound like
you're sort of hankering back
to those days.

667
00:35:17,567 --> 00:35:19,867
你口口声声说自己是个现代人，
但实际上……
You claim to be a modern man
but in actual fact...

668
00:35:19,900 --> 00:35:23,300
确实如此。
乡间B级路，你知道的，
就是那种情怀。
It's true.
The B road, you know,
it's that sort of thing.

669
00:35:23,333 --> 00:35:26,667
比如在米德赫斯特，
在英格兰南部的那些郡，
You know, Midhurst,
and southern counties
of England,

670
00:35:26,667 --> 00:35:28,567
在B级公路上兜风穿行，
就像老英剧《复仇者》里一样。
going around the B roads
like the avengers
or something.

671
00:35:28,667 --> 00:35:31,833
在那种路上开车，
是真真正正的纯粹驾驶乐趣。
There is a real pleasure,
a real joy in motoring there.

672
00:35:31,867 --> 00:35:34,900
当然了，你肯定深有体会，
毕竟你住在诺福克郡嘛！
And of course, you do have
a taste of that because
you live in Norfolk!

673
00:35:34,933 --> 00:35:38,767
是啊是啊，你把诺福克写得很精辟，
也很枯燥冗长……倒也没那么枯燥啦。
Yes, yes, you've written well
and turgidly about Norfolk...
Not turgidly exactly.

674
00:35:38,800 --> 00:35:41,533
呃，只是因为有一次，
我第一……倒不是我第一次去那儿，
Well, it was just that,
that time the first... Not the
first time I went there,

675
00:35:41,567 --> 00:35:45,267
但我还记得
就在不久前，
我开车沿着一条主干道走，
but I can remember
not that long ago,
driving along a main road,

676
00:35:45,300 --> 00:35:50,167
加满了油，
我把信用卡递给收银台的那位老兄，
filled it with petrol
and I gave the bloke in
the cash point my credit card,

677
00:35:50,200 --> 00:35:52,133
他居然直接把卡扔进了钱箱抽屉里！
he just put it in the till!

678
00:35:53,533 --> 00:35:56,200
“别别别，不是这么使的，
你应该拿它去刷卡啊！”
"No, no. No, no,
you're supposed to
swipe it."

679
00:35:56,233 --> 00:35:57,933
这里可是……（大笑）
This is... (LAUGHING)

680
00:35:57,967 --> 00:36:01,067
这里可是莲花跑车的故乡！
是个先进又高端的郡！
This is the home of Lotus.
It's an advanced
sophisticated county.

681
00:36:01,100 --> 00:36:03,867
你看吧，
刚才那个例子举得太烂了。
Now, you see,
that was a bad example.

682
00:36:03,900 --> 00:36:05,667
（结巴）行吧。
(STUTTERING) All right.

683
00:36:05,667 --> 00:36:08,000
不，那地方真是个神秘的郡。
No, it's a mysterious county.

684
00:36:08,033 --> 00:36:10,233
你走进一个古朴美丽的小村子，
到处都是那种，
You go to a beautiful
old-world village
with a, sort of,

685
00:36:10,267 --> 00:36:15,100
装有直棂窗、爬满常春藤的牧师公馆，
还有乡绅的宅邸，
mullion-windowed rectory
with ivy over it
and the squire's house

686
00:36:15,133 --> 00:36:16,267
以及漂亮的古老教堂。
and the beautiful old church.

687
00:36:16,300 --> 00:36:18,467
然后冷不丁竖着块牌子写着：
“改装直线加速赛”。
And then a sign saying,
"Hot-rodding".

688
00:36:18,500 --> 00:36:20,933
-你懂的，就是那种调调。
-拖拉机拔河赛！
-You know,
it's that sort of a thing.
-Tractor pull!

689
00:36:20,967 --> 00:36:23,800
而且他们还极其悲哀地
幻想自己是美国老铁红脖子。
And they imagine themselves
rather tragically to be
good old boys.

690
00:36:23,833 --> 00:36:27,400
他们开着引擎盖上贴着南方邦联星旗、
烂得快散架的野马，
They have these rotting
Mustangs with confederate
stars on the bonnet,

691
00:36:27,433 --> 00:36:33,300
满心期盼着分分钟会有个
嚼着烟草的警长咬在屁股后面追他们！
rather hoping there's gonna be
some tobacco-chewing sheriff
on their ass any minute!

692
00:36:33,333 --> 00:36:34,900
他们幻想着自己身在阿拉巴马，
They imagine
they're in Alabama,

693
00:36:34,933 --> 00:36:36,800
可悲哀的是，他们根本不是，
他们是在诺福克！
and it's tragic,
'cause they're not,
they're in Norfolk.

694
00:36:36,833 --> 00:36:38,400
根本没人会搭理你……
No one is gonna say...

695
00:36:38,433 --> 00:36:41,033
你跟警察说：
“我后备箱里带了私酿土炮”，人家根本无所谓！
Telling the police,
"I've got some moonshine
in the boot," it's fine!

696
00:36:41,067 --> 00:36:44,900
“别抓我，真是私酿烈酒，
我自己用土豆烤的！”
"No, it's moonshine,
I made it myself
out of potatoes!"

697
00:36:44,933 --> 00:36:47,933
不过我现在最感兴趣的是，
你开得怎么样？
What I'm most
interested in, though,
is how you got on?

698
00:36:47,967 --> 00:36:51,667
-我的天呐！
-开着那辆铃木Liana。
在赛道上感觉如何？
-Oh, hell!
-In the Suzuki Liana.
How was it out there?

699
00:36:51,700 --> 00:36:54,000
坦白讲，我玩得挺嗨的。
I have to say that I had fun.

700
00:36:54,033 --> 00:36:58,467
而且我自己感觉
开得比平时快多了，
And I seemed to myself
to be going faster
than I usually do,

701
00:36:58,500 --> 00:37:00,667
但天晓得我是不是
整整跑了四分钟！你根本没数，
but for all I know,
I did it in four minutes!
You just don't know,

702
00:37:00,667 --> 00:37:03,733
因为脑子里一片混乱……
这种开法完全是另一码事。
because your mind's in
a whirl... It's a totally
different way of doing things.

703
00:37:03,767 --> 00:37:05,233
你希望自己在圈速榜上排哪儿？
How would you like
to do on this?

704
00:37:05,267 --> 00:37:07,967
讲真，我希望能排在艾伦·戴维斯前面。
I'd like to be above
Alan Davies, I have to say.

705
00:37:08,000 --> 00:37:10,533
艾伦·戴维斯，《QI》里跟你搭伙同谋那位。
Alan Davies, your
co-conspirator on QI.

706
00:37:10,567 --> 00:37:14,167
所以这才是你的真正目标，
微湿赛道下的1分54秒。
So this is really your target,
1:54 on a mildly damp track.

707
00:37:14,200 --> 00:37:16,100
当时赛道情况到底怎么样？
What was the track like
out there?

708
00:37:16,133 --> 00:37:21,067
当时是……我希望你能写成
类似“略微潮湿”，或者你懂的那种……
It was... I'd like you to put
something like "slightly
moist", or you know...

709
00:37:21,100 --> 00:37:25,500
既然是你嘛，
那就“略微潮湿”吧。不过咱们来看看你跑得如何。
Because it's you,
slightly moist. But let's see
how you got on.

710
00:37:25,533 --> 00:37:27,467
你觉得那车怎么样？
What did you think
of the car?

711
00:37:27,500 --> 00:37:29,933
-弗莱：简直是天使，开起来太带劲了。
-绝对的。
-FRY: Angel. Joyous to drive.
-Absolutely.

712
00:37:29,967 --> 00:37:32,133
快看他，
瞧他那副蠢样简直像个傻缺！
Look at him,
doesn't he look a dick!

713
00:37:32,900 --> 00:37:34,667
真是够了！
Really!

714
00:37:34,667 --> 00:37:37,133
克拉克森：来，
这是整条赛道上最难的一个弯……
CLARKSON: Now,
that's the hardest
corner on the track...

715
00:37:38,433 --> 00:37:41,667
从这几处弯道加速冲出来……
Let's accelerate
out of these things...

716
00:37:41,667 --> 00:37:46,367
我看出来了，还真是，你说得对，
赛道确实有点湿。切入锤头弯，
I see, it is, you're right,
that is mildly moist.
Into the Hammerhead,

717
00:37:46,400 --> 00:37:50,100
还有这儿，你一把甩进去，
然后车头必然推头跑偏，看吧，果然推了。
and this one, as you flick
it in, and then it always runs
wide, which it has done.

718
00:37:50,133 --> 00:37:51,833
（惊呼）
(EXCLAIMS)

719
00:37:51,867 --> 00:37:53,400
漂亮！差点怼翻摄像师！
那可就真能上晚间新闻了。
Yes. Nearly into the
cameraman! That would
have been on the news.

720
00:37:53,433 --> 00:37:54,667
哎哟喂！
Oops!

721
00:37:56,800 --> 00:37:59,733
-噢，这下看着不错。
-天空真漂亮。
-Ooh, that looked good.
-That's a lovely sky.

722
00:37:59,767 --> 00:38:01,567
天色确实美极了。
That's a beautiful sky.

723
00:38:01,667 --> 00:38:03,667
进弯，来到甘邦弯了，
当年他差点在这儿
把车开翻。
In, and we've got Gambon,
where he nearly
rolled it over.

724
00:38:03,667 --> 00:38:06,100
差点在演邓布利多之前
就把邓布利多给干掉了。
Nearly killed Dumbledore
before he ever was.

725
00:38:07,300 --> 00:38:08,300
哇哦！
Whoa!

726
00:38:08,900 --> 00:38:10,400
好吧……
Well...

727
00:38:14,133 --> 00:38:17,667
-S·弗雷……
-哦。
-S. Fry...
-Oh.

728
00:38:17,667 --> 00:38:21,700
我想大家都同意，
刚才赛道的情况
算是微湿。
So, I think we're all
in agreement, that was
mildly moist, the track.

729
00:38:21,733 --> 00:38:27,500
所以就算和戴维斯那次一样，
行吧，
都是微湿……
So, we'll say it's the same
as Davies' one, okay,
mildly moist...

730
00:38:27,533 --> 00:38:30,033
你跑完了。
要想赢的话得跑进1分54秒……
And you did it.
You want 1:54 to beat...

731
00:38:30,667 --> 00:38:32,533
你的成绩是：1分……
In one minute...

732
00:38:32,567 --> 00:38:34,667
-54秒，
女士们先生们！
-噢，不！
-Fifty-four seconds,
ladies and gentlemen.
-Oh, no!

733
00:38:36,667 --> 00:38:38,033
唉，好吧！
Oh, well!

734
00:38:38,767 --> 00:38:41,533
这就很有意思了。
That is really interesting.

735
00:38:41,567 --> 00:38:44,200
这绝对是榜上
出现频率最高的成绩了，
对吧？
That's far and away
the most common time,
isn't it?

736
00:38:44,233 --> 00:38:47,300
雨天跑出1分54秒
是最常见的……
1.54 in the rain
is the most common...

737
00:38:47,333 --> 00:38:50,867
-按我们的规矩，
要是大晴天干地的话……
-对。
-What we say is,
if it were to be dry...
-Yeah.

738
00:38:50,900 --> 00:38:52,500
……成绩能扣掉整整四秒。
...you would take
four seconds off that.

739
00:38:52,533 --> 00:38:55,033
那你就能进1分50秒，
或者可能稍微再慢一点，
So, you would be in the 1:50
or maybe mildly down,

740
00:38:55,067 --> 00:38:58,800
估计只能扣三秒，
所以你还是比我慢，
这才是最重要的。
probably only three seconds,
so you're slower than me,
that's most important.

741
00:38:58,833 --> 00:39:01,333
-你能来真是太棒了。
-我也是，非常荣幸。
-It's been absolutely fabulous
having you here.
-As it has for me.

742
00:39:01,367 --> 00:39:04,200
-女士们先生们，
斯蒂芬·弗雷！
-非常感谢。
-Ladies and gentlemen,
Stephen Fry!
-Thank you very much.

743
00:39:12,833 --> 00:39:15,567
好了。好嘞。
Right. Right.

744
00:39:15,667 --> 00:39:17,233
回到房车的话题。
Back to the caravans.

745
00:39:17,267 --> 00:39:20,067
在节目早些时候，
我们看到那台
沃尔沃240旅行车，
Now, earlier on in the show,
we saw as the
Volvo 240 Estate,

746
00:39:20,100 --> 00:39:21,667
也就是房车的老朋友，
还记得吧，
the caravan's friend,
remember,

747
00:39:21,667 --> 00:39:23,800
冲上了跳台，
眼看就要飞跃那一排房车，
mounted the ramp,
and was about
to clear the caravans

748
00:39:23,833 --> 00:39:26,033
然后我们按下了暂停，
让大家都猜了猜结果。
and then we stopped the tape
and we all had a guess.

749
00:39:26,067 --> 00:39:27,767
大家普遍认同的观点是，
The general consensus
of opinion is that

750
00:39:27,800 --> 00:39:30,267
这台沃尔沃要么能
直接飞跃所有房车，
the Volvo is either gonna
clear all of the caravans

751
00:39:30,300 --> 00:39:33,000
要么就会极其狼狈地
一头从跳台上栽下去。
or kind of drop miserably
off the ramp.

752
00:39:33,033 --> 00:39:35,367
好消息是，答案马上揭晓。
Good news is, now we find out.

753
00:39:37,167 --> 00:39:40,567
哈蒙德：我们已经按照
约定俗成的规矩，
把房车排成了一排，
HAMMOND: So, we've lined up
our caravans in the
accepted manner,

754
00:39:40,667 --> 00:39:44,767
并严格符合规定，
在每辆车之间
留出了12英寸的间隙。
allowing the regulation,
12 inches of air space
in between each one.

755
00:39:48,200 --> 00:39:53,300
现在出场的是我们的
沃尔沃240旅行版，
还是GL型。
And here's our
Volvo 240 Estate,
the GL model.

756
00:39:53,333 --> 00:39:57,733
无线电声音：
三、二、一，走！
VOICE ON RADIO:
Three, two, one, go!

757
00:40:00,700 --> 00:40:02,600
车冲出去了！
And he's off!

758
00:40:02,633 --> 00:40:05,067
现在我得提醒各位一句，
拖着房车行驶的时候，
国家法定限速
Now, I should remind you,
the national speed limit
when you turn your caravan

759
00:40:05,100 --> 00:40:07,700
当然是每小时50英里，
而我们绝对会
严格遵守这一条。
is of course, 50 miles an hour
and we will be
sticking to that.

760
00:40:07,733 --> 00:40:09,767
我们虽然也跟大家一样
喜欢找乐子，
We like a laugh,
as much as the next person,

761
00:40:09,800 --> 00:40:12,300
但这并不意味着
你就可以胡来。
but that doesn't mean
you have to be reckless.

762
00:40:20,133 --> 00:40:22,433
（观众笑声）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

763
00:40:26,433 --> 00:40:27,733
干得漂亮！
Well done!

764
00:40:28,500 --> 00:40:29,733
哇哦！
Wow!

765
00:40:31,033 --> 00:40:34,833
刚才简直是艺术！绝对是艺术！
话说，谁还想
再看一遍？
That was art! That is art!
In fact, who wants
to see it again?

766
00:40:34,867 --> 00:40:36,667
-众人：想！
-那就再来一遍。
-ALL: Yes!
-Go on then.

767
00:40:51,267 --> 00:40:54,000
哎呀，看来是我错了！
我彻底猜错了！
Oh, dear, so I was wrong!
I was wrong!

